    "INDEX0<SEP>Describe how to prepare the given food in your own words. Note down the ingredients you will need and the steps you will take to prepare them.\n\nChewy Chocolate Chip Cookies<SEP>Ingredients:\n- 1 cup of unsalted butter, cold\n- 1 cup of granulated sugar\n- 1/2 cup of brown sugar\n- 2 large eggs\n- 2 teaspoons of vanilla extract\n- 2 1/4 cups of all-purpose flour\n- 1 teaspoon of baking soda\n- 1/2 teaspoon of salt\n- 2 cups of semi-sweet chocolate chips\n- 1 cup of pecans or walnuts, optional\n\nSteps to prepare the ingredients:\n1. Preheat your oven to 350°F (175°C) and line a baking sheet with parchment paper.\n2. In a large mixing bowl, cream together the cold butter and sugars until light and fluffy. This usually takes about 3-4 minutes.\n3. Add the eggs one at a time, beating well after each addition. Then, stir in the vanilla extract.\n4. In a separate bowl, whisk together the flour, baking soda, and salt. Gradually add the dry ingredients to the wet ingredients and mix until just combined.\n5. Stir in the chocolate chips and nuts (if using) until evenly distributed.\n6. Using a spoon or cookie scoop, drop the dough onto the prepared baking sheet, spacing them about 2 inches apart.\n7. Bake the cookies in the preheated oven for 10-12 minutes, or until the edges are lightly golden brown. The centers will still look soft, but they will set as they cool.\n8. Let the cookies cool on the baking sheet for a few minutes before transferring them to a wire rack to cool completely.\n9. Enjoy your chewy chocolate chip cookies! Additionally, for a chewier texture, you can try using a mixer for creaming the butter and sugar, or incorporating a few tablespoons of milk into the dough. Experiment with different types of chocolate chips or nuts, such as white chocolate or macadamia nuts, to make the recipe your own. Remember to handle raw eggs and baking ingredients safely to maintain food safety standards.": 3.15625,
    "INDEX0<SEP>Describe how to prepare the given food in your own words. Note down the ingredients you will need and the steps you will take to prepare them.\n\nChewy Chocolate Chip Cookies<SEP>You will need the following ingredients:\n- 1 cup of unsalted butter, chilled\n- 1 cup of granulated sugar\n- 1/2 cup of brown sugar\n- 2 large eggs\n- 2 teaspoons of vanilla extract\n- 2 1/4 cups of all-purpose flour\n- 1 teaspoon of baking soda\n- 1/2 teaspoon of salt\n- 2 cups of semi-sweet chocolate chips\n- 1 cup of pecans or walnuts, optional\n\nSteps you will take to prepare them:\n1. Preheat your oven to 350°F (175°C) and line a baking sheet with parchment paper.\n2. In a large mixing bowl, cream together the cold butter and sugars until light and fluffy. This usually takes about 3-4 minutes.\n3. Add the eggs one at a time, beating well after each addition. Then, stir in the vanilla extract.\n4. In a separate bowl, whisk together the flour, baking soda, and salt. Gradually add the dry ingredients to the wet ingredients and mix until just combined.\n5. Stir in the chocolate chips and nuts (if using) until evenly distributed.\n6. Using a spoon or cookie scoop, drop the dough onto the prepared baking sheet, spacing them about 2 inches apart.\n7. Bake the cookies in the preheated oven for 10-12 minutes, or until the edges are lightly golden brown. The centers will still look soft, but they will set as they cool.\n8. Let the cookies cool on the baking sheet for a few minutes before transferring them to a wire rack to cool completely.\n9. Enjoy your chewy chocolate chip cookies!\n\nAdditional Tips:\n- For a chewier texture, use cold butter and do not overbake the cookies.\n- Try using different types of chocolate chips, such as milk or white chocolate, for a unique flavor.\n- Experiment with adding other mix-ins, such as dried fruit or toffee bits, to customize your cookies.": 3.984375,
    "INDEX1<SEP>Describe how to prepare the given food in your own words. Note down the ingredients you will need and the steps you will take to prepare them.\n\nChewy Chocolate Chip Cookies<SEP>You will need the following ingredients:\n- 200 grams of unsalted butter, chilled and cubed\n- 100 grams of granulated sugar\n- 50 grams of brown sugar\n- 2 large eggs\n- 2 teaspoons of vanilla extract\n- 250 grams of all-purpose flour\n- 1/2 teaspoon of baking soda\n- 1/4 teaspoon of salt\n- 200 grams of semi-sweet chocolate chips\n- 100 grams of pecans or walnuts, optional\n\nSteps you will take to prepare them:\n1. Preheat your oven to 180°C (350°F) and line a baking sheet with parchment paper.\n2. In a large mixing bowl, cream together the cold butter and sugars until light and fluffy. This usually takes about 3-4 minutes.\n3. Add the eggs one at a time, beating well after each addition. Then, stir in the vanilla extract.\n4. In a separate bowl, whisk together the flour, baking soda, and salt. Gradually add the dry ingredients to the wet ingredients and mix until just combined.\n5. Stir in the chocolate chips and nuts (if using) until evenly distributed.\n6. Using a spoon or cookie scoop, drop the dough onto the prepared baking sheet, spacing them about 2 inches apart.\n7. Bake the cookies in the preheated oven for 12-15 minutes, or until the edges are lightly golden brown. The centers will still look soft, but they will set as they cool.\n8. Let the cookies cool on the baking sheet for a few minutes before transferring them to a wire rack to cool completely.\n9. Enjoy your chewy chocolate chip cookies!\n\nAdditional Tips:\n- For a chewier texture, use cold butter and do not overbake the cookies.\n- Try using different types of chocolate chips, such as milk or white chocolate, for a unique flavor.\n- Experiment with adding other mix-ins, such as dried fruit or toffee bits, to customize your cookies.\n- Store the cookies in an airtight container at room temperature for up to a week, or freeze them for longer storage.\n- Each cookie has approximately 60 calories, 3 grams of fat, 7 grams of carbohydrates, and 1 gram of protein.": 3.34375,
